      "body": "## Motivation\n\nOn `amd_march`, the ROCm AOT build accepts `gfx1100` and `gfx1201` but not the other RDNA3 / RDNA4 discrete parts:\n\n- gfx1101 (Navi 32, e.g. RX 7800 XT / W7800)\n- gfx1102 (Navi 33, e.g. RX 7600)\n- gfx1200 (Navi 44, e.g. RX 9060 XT)\n\nFor those, the build stops immediately:\n\n```\n$ AMDGPU_TARGET=gfx1101 python setup_rocm.py build_ext --inplace\nError: Unsupported GPU architecture 'gfx1101'. Expected one of: ['gfx942', 'gfx950', 'gfx1100', 'gfx1151', 'gfx1201', 'gfx1250']\n```\n\nThey are the same ISA families as gfx1100 / gfx1201: wave32, and `is_rdna_supported()` already matches `gfx11*` / `gfx120*`. They need no code change beyond the allowlist. This is the smallest piece of the RDNA plan in #46900.\n\n## Modifications\n\nAdd `gfx1101`, `gfx1102` and `gfx1200` to `supported_archs` in `python/sglang/kernels/aot/setup_rocm.py`. Nothing else changes, and the build is unchanged for every target that was already accepted.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n**Build.** `rocm/pytorch:rocm7.2.3_ubuntu24.04_py3.12_pytorch_release_2.10.0`, no GPU in the container, so `AMDGPU_TARGET` is used as given. Offload bundles were read back from `common_ops*.so` with `llvm-objdump --offloading`, run on a copy.\n\n| `AMDGPU_TARGET` | before | this PR | bundles |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `gfx1101` | `Error: Unsupported GPU architecture` | rc=0 | gfx1101 |\n| `gfx1102` | same error | rc=0 | gfx1102 |\n| `gfx1200` | same error | rc=0 | gfx1200 |\n| `gfx1100;gfx1101;gfx1102;gfx1200;gfx1201` | same error | rc=0 | all five |\n\n**Runtime.** I don't have gfx1101/1102/1200 hardware. The five-arch fat binary above was installed and the AOT kernel tests were run on the two RDNA GPUs I do have, one pytest per file:\n\n| test | gfx1100 (W7900D) | gfx1201 (R9700) |\n|---|---|---|\n| test_activation | 945 passed | 945 passed |\n| test_apply_token_bitmask_inplace | 1 passed | 1 passed |\n| test_moe_topk_softmax | 744 passed | 744 passed |\n| test_moe_topk_sigmoid | 774 passed | 774 passed |\n| test_dsv4_norm_rope | 16 passed | 16 passed |\n| test_moe_align | 4368 passed, 72 skipped | 4368 passed, 72 skipped |\n| test_topk | 157 failed, 5 passed (same on unmodified `amd_march`, see below) | 157 failed, 5 passed (same on unmodified `amd_march`) |\n\n`test_topk` fails the same way on unmodified `amd_march` on both GPUs: 157 failed / 5 passed. It is not related to this change. The cause is that `include/hip/dsa_topk_coop.cuh` hard-codes `kWaveSize = 64`. `main` fixed that in #41687, and I'll open a separate backport of it to `amd_march`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nN/A (build allowlist only).\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [ ] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (Build-script allowlist; verified by the builds above.)\n- [x] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). (No doc change needed.)\n- [x] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results. (See above.)\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40617430344](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40617430344)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40617430429](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40617430429)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40617430437](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40617430437)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
